---
title: DMA2D - Chrom-Art graphics accelerator, nothing to wire
---
%% ON-CHIP ONLY. No pins. Moves and blends pixels without the CPU.
%% Typically works on framebuffers living in the on-board SDRAM behind FMC,
%% then LTDC scans those framebuffers out to the LCD.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1"]
        CPU["Cortex-M4 core"]
        D2D["DMA2D engine"]
        MODE["Modes: register-to-memory fill, memory-to-memory copy, blend, convert"]
    end

    subgraph SDRAM["On-board SDRAM via FMC"]
        FG["Foreground layer"]
        BG["Background layer"]
        FB["Output framebuffer"]
    end

    LCD["LTDC to on-board LCD"]

    CPU -->|"set up transfer"| D2D
    MODE --- D2D
    FG --> D2D
    BG --> D2D
    D2D --> FB
    FB --> LCD
